# zero-platform

The Waveshare Zero family, sold as the RP2040-Zero and RP2350-Zero mini
boards: a bare chip on a 23.5 by 18 mm board with a USB-C socket on the native
port, a WS2812B RGB LED on GP16, BOOT and RESET keys, and every other GPIO on
its edge -- GP0 to GP15 and GP26 to GP29 on the 23-pin header, the rest on
castellated pads.

rp2040_zero derives from pico and rp2350_zero from pico2-arm. Neither binds a
provider: there is no panel or sensor to describe, and nothing in modules/mm
drives the WS2812B yet. What the boards change is in the Pico bridge's board
table, which corrects the defaults their vendor ancestors set for a Pico.
